Fix for vllm-project/vllm-ascend#11548 on vllm-ascend releases/v0.23.0.

    [Bug]: vllm ascend sleep mode has a bug that wake up make expert shape wrong
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/issues/11548
    Still open upstream as of 2026-07-27 with no fix merged, so this is a local fix.

NPUWorker.wake_up() guards its expert-weight transpose on the wrong dimension: w13 is
[E, 2I, H] (hidden_size at dim 2) and w2 is [E, H, I] (hidden_size at dim 1), but the
two branches had those indices swapped. Weights restored from sleep in NPU layout were
therefore transposed a second time, and the first inference after sleep -> wake_up
failed on mismatched input/weight shapes. With the indices corrected the transpose only
fires for weights still in canonical layout, i.e. those freshly pushed by weight sync.

diff --git a/vllm_ascend/worker/worker.py b/vllm_ascend/worker/worker.py
index c2e0e8f..1665785 100644
--- a/vllm_ascend/worker/worker.py
+++ b/vllm_ascend/worker/worker.py
@@ -252,7 +252,7 @@ class NPUWorker(WorkerBase):
         model = self.model_runner.model
         if self.vllm_config.quant_config is None and (tags is None or "weights" in tags):
             for name, param in model.named_parameters():
-                if "w2_weight" in name and param.shape[2] == hidden_size:
+                if "w2_weight" in name and param.shape[1] == hidden_size:
                     parts = name.split(".")
                     param_name = parts[-1]
                     parent_module = model.get_submodule(".".join(parts[:-1]))
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ class NPUWorker(WorkerBase):
                     w2_data = param.transpose(1, 2)
                     w2_data = torch.nn.Parameter(w2_data, requires_grad=False)
                     setattr(parent_module, param_name, w2_data)
-                elif "w13_weight" in name and param.shape[1] == hidden_size:
+                elif "w13_weight" in name and param.shape[2] == hidden_size:
                     parts = name.split(".")
                     param_name = parts[-1]
                     parent_module = model.get_submodule(".".join(parts[:-1]))
